:name: R2 rung 3 - execution trace, to PROVE the window handlers really fire
:description: Without this, rung 3 passing only shows that the call chains
:description: returned the right numbers - it would not show that the register
:description: file ever overflowed. This traces every retired PC;
:description: emulator/renode/tests/count-window-vectors.mjs counts entries to the
:description: six window vectors at VECBASE+0x000/040/080/0C0/100/140.
:description:
:description: The caller MUST set $trace to an ABSOLUTE output path first - Renode
:description: 1.16.1 will not create a trace file from a repo-relative path:
:description:   $trace=@C:/path/to/repo/emulator/renode/tests/logs/r2-rung3.trace
:description: count-window-vectors.mjs does that for you; just run
:description:   node emulator/renode/tests/count-window-vectors.mjs

using sysbus
mach create "r2-rung3-trace"
machine LoadPlatformDescription @emulator/renode/platforms/esp32s2-sesame.repl
sysbus LoadELF @firmware/probes/build/r2-rung3-window.elf
cpu CreateExecutionTracing "tracer" $trace "PC"
emulation RunFor "0.0005"
cpu DisableExecutionTracing
echo "### traced"
sysbus ReadBytes 0x3FFD0000 128
quit
